[checkpoints/tinystories-v2 p0 s0] Ben had a small boat. He took it to the lake and put it in the water. He watched the boat float. He saw the duck swim with it. He wanted to catch it.
He went near the duck. He tried to get his boat. But the duck did not like that. It pecked at Ben's boat. Ben was sad. He cried.
"Hey, stop that!" a man shouted. He was the owner of the duck. He ran to Ben and took the boat away from him. "This is my duck. You are a bad boy."
The man was angry. He said, "You should not take things that are not yours. You should not bother the ducks. They have feelings too. You should be nice to them."
Ben was sorry. He said, "I am sorry, mister. I did not know. I just wanted to see the ducks. They are so pretty."
The man said, "You cannot come near the pond again. The pond is dangerous. The ducks are scared. You have to leave them alone."
Ben nodded. He said, "OK, mister. I will leave them alone. I will go home."
Ben walked back to his mom. He hugged her. He told her what happened. She hugged him back. She said, "I am proud of you, Ben. You are a good boy. But next time, please ask before you touch the animals. And be careful of the pond."
Ben smiled. He said, "Thank you, mom. I love you. Can we still watch the ducks?"
His mom said, "Of course, Ben. We can watch the ducks again. But only for a little while. Then we have to go home."

[checkpoints/tinystories-v2 p0 s1] Ben had a small boat. He took it to the lake and put it in the water. He watched it float and spin. He saw other boats and fish too. He smiled and clapped his hands.
"Look, Anna, there are seasons!" he said. "It is snow, snow, snow, and flowers. It is very nice."
Anna nodded. She liked snow too. She liked how it made her skin feel warm and soft. She looked at the seasons and saw that they were different. She liked them all, but she liked Ben more. He was nice and kind.
"OK, Ben, you can be the seasons too," she said. "But you have to be careful. There might be thorns or sharp stones. And don't touch the fish. They are wild animals."
They played some games in the seasons. They made snowballs and threw them at each other. They had fun. They laughed and sang and made snow angels. They forgot about the time.
Soon, the sun started to set. The seasons changed. The seasons became faded. The water turned white and cold. The trees turned black. The birds flew away. The rabbits ran into the water. The birds flew to a tree.
"Bye, Anna, you are very pretty," Ben said. "You have a pretty hat. I like your hat."
"Bye, Ben, you are very nice," Anna said. "Thank you for playing with me. You are my friend."
They hugged and smiled. They felt warm and happy. They forgot about the snow. They enjoyed the seasons. They liked each other.

[checkpoints/tinystories-v2 p0 s2] Ben had a small boat. He took it to the lake and put it in the water. He watched the boat float. He saw other boats in the water. They were different colors and sizes. Ben liked them all.
