They ran back to their mom and dad. They told them what happened. Mom and dad gave them some bread and cheese. They said, "We are sorry, kids. We should not throw rocks in the lake. That was dangerous. The lake is deep and dirty. We will clean it up."
They ate their food and drank their milk. They felt better. They went back to the lake. They played with the boat. They made the lake go fast. They were happy.

