[checkpoints/stories-v3 p0 s0] Ben had a small boat. He took it to the lake and put it in the water. He pushed it with his hand and watched it float. He was very happy.
"Can I sail your boat, Tom?" Sam asked.
Tom was not nice. He said, "No, this is my boat. You can't sail it. Go away!"
Sam felt sad. He wanted to play with Tom. He thought of a plan. He waited until Tom was not looking. Then he took the boat and ran away.
Tom saw that his boat was gone. He was angry. He shouted, "Hey, give me back my boat! That is my boat!"
He ran after Sam. He tried to catch him. But Sam was fast. He ran across the grass and the sand. He did not see the big rock. He tripped and fell. The boat flew out of his hands. It landed on the ground.
Tom caught up with Sam. He picked up his boat. He saw that it was dirty and wet. He was very mad. He said, "You are a bad boy! You broke my boat! You hurt me and my boat!"
Sam was sorry. He said, "I'm sorry, Tom. I just wanted to sail your boat. I didn't mean to break it. Please don't be mad at me."
Tom looked at Sam. He saw that Sam was sorry. He said, "It's okay, Sam. I forgive you. But you have to be careful next time. And you have to ask before you take something. And you have to help me fix my boat."
Sam nodded. He said, "Thank you, Tom. You are a good friend. Can we still play with the boat together?"
Tom smiled. He said, "Yes, we can. But you have to be gentle with the boat. And you have to share with me."
They hugged. They went to find some tape and glue.

[checkpoints/stories-v3 p0 s1] Ben had a small boat. He took it to the lake and rowed away. He did not care about Mia or anyone else. He only cared about his boat and his adventure.
Mia was sad and angry. She did not like Ben anymore. She stayed on the shore and watched him go. She wished he would be nicer and share his boat with her.
But Ben did not stop. He sailed further and farther from Mia. He saw many things and met many people. He saw big mountains and deep seas. He saw colorful birds and strange fish. He saw scary monsters and dark caves. He was having fun and forgot about Mia.
But then, something bad happened. A big wave came and knocked Ben off his boat. His boat flipped over and sank into the water. Ben was scared and cold. He cried for help.
Mia heard Ben's cry. She looked up and saw him sinking in the lake. She felt sorry for him. She ran to get her friends. They were Tom and Lily. They had a boat too. It was smaller and faster than Ben's boat.
They saw Ben in the water and his boat under the waves. They wanted to rescue him. They threw their boats at the waves and made loud noises. They hoped someone would hear them and help.
But no one came. The waves were too strong. The boats could not reach Ben. Ben could not swim. He could not breathe. He could not call for help. He was gone.
The end.

